# MonsterBox Yard Theater — Halloween night schedule (America/Chicago)
# Install:  crontab -e  and paste the block below (or see README).
# Any one node can conduct the whole yard via the orchestration API.
#
# BEFORE INSTALLING (verified 2026-08-16, both are load-bearing):
#   mkdir -p /home/remote/yard-theater-logs
#     Without it every line here fails at the redirect and the command never
#     runs at all — cron cannot create the directory for you.
#   timedatectl | grep 'Time zone'   ->  must read America/Chicago
#     cron fires on local time, so these 18:30 / 20:47 / 02:00 slots are only
#     the times you mean if the node's clock agrees.
#
# The `cd /home/remote/MonsterBox &&` on every line is REQUIRED. cron runs with
# cwd=$HOME and PATH=/usr/bin:/bin, so without the cd, node resolves the script
# against /home/remote and dies with MODULE_NOT_FOUND. (Proven with a real
# temporary cron entry, not assumed: /usr/bin/node is on cron's PATH, and both
# scripts run clean under `env -i`. The ElevenLabs key is read from
# /etc/monsterbox/elevenlabs.key, which needs no interactive environment.)
#
# Rehearse any line before trusting it — --dry-run makes no sound and no calls:
#   node scripts/yard-theater/perform.mjs moments/dusk-ceremony.json --dry-run

# The Dusk Ceremony — the yard wakes (sunset in Coralville Oct 31 is ~6:05pm; dusk ~6:30)
30 18 31 10 * cd /home/remote/MonsterBox && node scripts/yard-theater/perform.mjs moments/dusk-ceremony.json >> /home/remote/yard-theater-logs/theater.log 2>&1

# Thomas — once. An odd minute, deep in the evening, when the yard is busy.
47 20 31 10 * cd /home/remote/MonsterBox && node scripts/yard-theater/perform.mjs moments/thomas.json >> /home/remote/yard-theater-logs/theater.log 2>&1

# Night Memory — harvest the night's real conversations into the Yard Registry (2am Nov 1).
# The && is deliberate: the PHI suite gates the harvest, so a scrubber that has
# regressed can never publish a real child's surname to the knowledge base.
# The chain is wrapped in a subshell so the redirect covers BOTH commands. Without
# the parentheses `>>` binds only to the last command of the && chain, so a scrub
# test that trips the PHI gate writes its reason to a discarded stdout and the
# harvest log is simply empty — the one night you would need to know why.
0 2 1 11 * cd /home/remote/MonsterBox && (node scripts/night-memory/scrub-test.mjs && node scripts/night-memory/harvest.mjs --hours 12) >> /home/remote/yard-theater-logs/harvest.log 2>&1

# Optional: October weekend rehearsal ceremony (Fri+Sat evenings in October)
# 30 18 * 10 5,6 cd /home/remote/MonsterBox && node scripts/yard-theater/perform.mjs moments/dusk-ceremony.json >> /home/remote/yard-theater-logs/theater.log 2>&1
